#: buildVars.py:19
msgid ""
"FreeRadio is an internet radio add-on for NVDA that provides seamless access "
"to thousands of stations via the Radio Browser open directory. It features a "
"fully accessible station browser with search, country filter, favourites "
"management, and per-station audio profiles. Playback is handled by a "
"prioritised backend chain (BASS, VLC, PotPlayer, Windows Media Player) with "
"support for volume control, audio effects, output device selection, and "
"simultaneous audio mirroring to a second device. Additional features include "
"instant and scheduled recording, sleep and alarm timers, automatic ICY "
"metadata announcements, Shazam-based music recognition, and a liked-songs "
"log. All controls and shortcuts are designed for NVDA accessibility."
msgstr ""

#: buildVars.py:26
msgid ""
"\n"
"**Fixed**\n"
"- **ICY \"Now Playing\" titles containing an apostrophe were truncated.** "
"The `StreamTitle` regex in `radioPlayer.py` stopped at the first `'` it "
"found, so any title with an apostrophe (e.g. *\"Don't Stop Believin'\"*) was "
"cut short. The parser now matches up to the closing `';` delimiter that ICY "
"metadata actually uses, so apostrophes inside the title no longer break the "
"match.\n"
"- Added: **Liked song context menu (Liked Songs Tab)**\n"
"- Right-click a station (or press the Applications key / Shift+F10) to bring "
"up a new context menu with quick actions\n"
"- Fixed: rewind/fast-forward stopped working after pausing and resuming\n"
"  playback. Pausing and resuming advanced the internal playback generation\n"
"  counter twice without re-syncing the time-shift buffer's own counter,\n"
"  so the buffer was permanently (and incorrectly) treated as stale for\n"
"  the rest of the session.\n"
"- Fixed: on HLS (.m3u8) stations, rewinding or fast-forwarding could land\n"
"  at the wrong point in time, and the \"N seconds behind live\" readout\n"
"  could show inconsistent or even negative values. The buffered-duration\n"
"  estimate was based on wall-clock time since capture started, which\n"
"  drifts from the actual amount of audio captured on HLS stations\n"
"  (manifest polling delays, segment-fetch latency, and bursty catch-up\n"
"  downloads all throw it off). Buffered duration for HLS is now computed\n"
"  from each segment's own declared duration, matching what is actually\n"
"  in the buffer.\n"
"\n"
"- Improved: trimming the old end of an HLS time-shift buffer now always\n"
"  drops whole segments instead of an estimated byte count, avoiding a\n"
"  rare risk of cutting a segment in half and producing a corrupt tail.\n"
"- **Time-shift (rewind) buffer could silently stop engaging, even after re-"
"enabling it.** `rewind_timeshift()` gates on two internal generation "
"counters staying in sync; a few code paths (station launch, resume-from-"
"pause, a successful stall reconnect) correctly re-synced them, but "
"`set_timeshift_enabled()` did not. If playback generation advanced elsewhere "
"(e.g. a brief stream stall/reconnect) without a matching sync, rewind would "
"permanently report \"not enough buffered audio,\" regardless of wait time, "
"and toggling time-shift off/on for the same station could not fix it — only "
"switching stations (which goes through the syncing path) sometimes did. "
"`set_timeshift_enabled()` now re-syncs the buffer generation after "
"(re)starting capture, closing that gap.\n"
msgstr ""
